<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Delhi Sultanate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Delhi Sultanate was a series of Muslim dynasties that ruled much of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> between the early thirteenth and early sixteenth centuries. It repelled Mongol incursions from the Chagatai realm, suffered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-delhi-1398">sack of Delhi</a> in 1398, and ended when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> sultan at Panipat in 1526, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate.jpg" alt="Delhi Sultanate" width="320" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maps created from DEMIS Mapserver, which are public domain. Koba-chan Territorial area: पाटलिपुत्र (talk), per Schwar... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Mamluk_Dynasty.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
